# VDX Design

This is a thin entry point. The canonical instructions live in two files
inside this repo — read them when activating this rule:

1. **`skills/vdx-design/SKILL.md`** — the full skill: when to trigger,
   theme loading, boilerplate, token usage rules, A/B decision flow, and
   reference docs index.

2. **`skills/vdx-design/workflows/scaffold-and-bundle.md`** — the
   scaffold-and-bundle workflow: how to set up a new site under
   `<target>/src/` and how to ship it as a single `<target>/view/index.html`
   via `node lib/bundle.js <target>`.

## Quick triggers

| User says | Read & follow |
|---|---|
| "Build a samsung-kr page", "Use the `<theme-id>` theme" | `skills/vdx-design/SKILL.md` |
| "Scaffold a vdx site at `<dir>`" | `scaffold-and-bundle.md` → Scaffold steps |
| "Bundle `<dir>`" / "다 만들었어, 하나로 묶어" | `scaffold-and-bundle.md` → Bundle steps |
| Has a meaningful taste choice between two designs | `SKILL.md` → Decision flow (`vdx-decide`) |

## Hard rules

- Never hardcode hex/px values in generated CSS — always `var(--vdx-…)`.
- The single-file deliverable for end users is `<target>/view/index.html`
  (CSS + JS inlined). Never tell a user to ship a multi-file site.
- Don't add npm dependencies. The project uses Node built-ins only.
